ABC also scheduled a special 20/20 episode called "Idaho Justice" to air on September 5 and stream the next day on Hulu.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:32.100
Just as the public was revisiting the tragedy, the man convicted of the crimes forced his way back into the headlines.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:37.600
The case file shows some of the strategies that original defense team tried to use before the plea.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:42.100
At one point, his attorneys alleged that he was diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.700
The judge pushed back hard on that specific claim.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:49.800
Judge Hippler stated he had never seen any odd behavior from the defendant across months of hearings.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.300
The judge noted that by all accounts, the defendant is highly-functioning.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:19:01.200
He ruled that a jury would not be allowed to hear testimony about an autism diagnosis unless Kohberger actually took the stand himself.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:05.500
Now, the defendant is arguing the legal guidance he received was completely flawed.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:12.000
He claims the false promises from his counsel led to a gross misrepresentation of what a life sentence would actually look like.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.900
We also know the original defense team made moves that significantly extended the timeline.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:20.100
Early in the process, Kohberger waived his right to a speedy trial.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:24.000
His attorney at the time cited the need for additional time to prepare the defense.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.400
Now, the new filing argues that preparation was completely inadequate.

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:32.000
Read the file, and you see a defendant trying to dismantle his own defense strategy piece by piece.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:37.200
The handwritten petition goes far beyond just complaining about bad legal advice.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.900
The motion further alleges that the plea was not made voluntarily.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:46.000
In the criminal justice system, an admission of guilt has to be a free and independent choice.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:51.300
If a judge determines that standard was not met, the entire agreement is thrown into question.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:55.100
The ultimate goal of this post-conviction maneuver is absolute.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.600
The defense requests the court to invalidate the guilty plea entirely.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:03.600
They are not asking for a modified sentence or a transfer to a different maximum-security facility.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:08.000
They want the judge to completely erase the admission of guilt from the official record.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.800
If the court actually agrees to grant this request, the legal landscape shifts overnight.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:16.100
The four consecutive life sentences would immediately disappear.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:20.500
The waiver of appeals he signed would be tossed out right along with the rest of the paperwork.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.900
The state of Idaho would be forced to take the entire homicide prosecution back to square one.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:29.900
That means prosecutors would have to prepare for the massive capital trial they thought they avoided.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:34.600
The victims' families would have to sit in a courtroom and listen to weeks of grueling cross-examinations.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:38.800
The legal finality they were promised after the sentencing hearing would be completely undone.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.700
A finalized capital murder case does not just reopen quietly.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:48.900
State prosecutors now have to defend a conviction they thought was permanently locked in place by a signed waiver.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.700
The scrutiny has shifted away from the touch DNA and the cellular data.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:59.100
Now, the microscope is pointed directly at the closed-door negotiations and the actions of the original defense team.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:04.100
The presiding judge now has to weigh the signed waiver against these new claims of coercion.

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:10.400
The court will have to determine if the original defense team actually crossed a line, or if the defendant simply changed his mind.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:14.100
We are waiting to see if the legal system will actually let him take it all back.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:18.800
That July 2026 motion to withdraw the plea remains pending on the court docket.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:25.200
The legal system moves slowly, especially when a defendant tries to completely unravel a finalized capital agreement.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:29.000
The state is standing its ground and defending the original conviction.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:33.300
Prosecutors are absolutely refusing to let the admission of guilt just slip away.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:38.100
The court has not yet ruled on the specific claims of coercion and ineffective counsel.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:43.200
A judge still needs to evaluate the serious accusations leveled against the original defense attorneys.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:48.400
They have to weigh the handwritten petition against the official transcript of the change of plea hearing.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:52.000
Until a formal ruling is handed down, the convictions are locked in place.

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:57.200
The final legal resolution of the King Road homicides now rests entirely in the hands of the judge.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:01.400
They have the authority to uphold the waiver or throw the entire plea deal out the window.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:06.000
The Goncalves family has expressed confidence he will get the death penalty if there is a trial.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:11.000
We will just have to wait and see how the justice system handles this unprecedented reversal.

